<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's NLCF seeks 262,500 tonnes of corn.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's NLCF seeks 262,500 tonnes of corn.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's National Livestock Cooperatives Federation (NLCF) has invited tenders for a total of 262,500 tonnes of U.S. No.3 yellow corn, traders said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>Traders said NLCF divided tenders into five positions, each of which totalls 52,500 tonnes.</p>
<p>For position one and two, it included Chinese corn as an acceptable origin. But each of the two positions would be split into 20,000 tonnes to Inchon, 20,000 tonnes to Ulsan and 12,000 tonnes to Kunsan, they said.</p>
<p>It also included Argentine maize as an acceptable origin for position three, four and five, they said.</p>
<p>It would recieve both offers for basis and flat.  </p>
<p>Details for the tender are as follow:</p>
<p> POSITION   TONNE   ETA	    SHIPMENT</p>
<p>    One     52,500  April 20  Mar 20-Apr 8 (PNW)</p>
<p>					Mar 1-20 (U.S. Gulf)</p>
<p>					Mar 27-Apr 15 (China)</p>
<p>    Two     52,500  April 25  Mar 25-Apr 13 (PNW)</p>
<p>					Mar 6-25 (U.S. Gulf)</p>
<p>					Apr 1-15 (China)</p>
<p>    Three   52,500  June 20   May 20-Jun 8 (PNW)</p>
<p>					May 1-20 (U.S. Gulf)</p>
<p>					Apr 26-May 15 (Argentina)</p>
<p>    Four    52,500  July 30   Jun 29-July 18 (PNW)</p>
<p>					Jun 10-29 (U.S. Gulf)</p>
<p>					Jun 5-24 (Argentina)</p>
<p>    Five    52,500  Aug 15    July 15-Aug 3 (PNW)</p>
<p>					Jun 26-July 15 (U.S. Gulf)</p>
<p>					Jun 21-July 10 (Argentina)</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
